    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26887" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŏcātōrĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to letting</i> or <i>hiring out</i>: locatorius, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μισθωσιμαῖος</span>, Gloss. Philox.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">locatoria provincia,</span>”
				<i>where one will be a mere letter out</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 15, 9, 1</span></i>
			; Orell. <i>N. cr</i>.</div>
